WEBVTT

00:00:02.369 --> 00:00:05.827
Captain's Log,
Stardate 41242.4:

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:07.772
Our last assignment
has taken us

00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:10.275
into the remote
Omicron Theta star system

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:14.747
home of our android crew member
Lieutenant Commander Data.

00:00:14.781 --> 00:00:17.272
Although we are due
at our next assignment

00:00:17.317 --> 00:00:19.842
I have decided
to visit Data's home planet

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:22.411
for a few hours
in the hopes of unraveling

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:24.719
some of the mystery
of his beginnings.

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:27.420
Sir, we are now 20 minutes
from Omicron Theta.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.757
Mark.

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:30.228
Stand by for subwarp.

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:33.096
Head for standard orbit
of Data's planet.

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:35.465
I wonder why Data
hasn't come up here.

00:00:35.502 --> 00:00:37.367
He said he wanted to be alone.

00:00:37.404 --> 00:00:38.769
Perhaps this is

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:41.273
a bigger moment for him
than we thought.

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:44.003
Ah...

00:00:44.044 --> 00:00:47.343
ah...

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:48.972
Data.

00:00:49.015 --> 00:00:51.449
...choo!

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:53.384
What are you doing?

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.752
Sneezing.

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:57.518
Have you got a cold?

00:00:57.557 --> 00:00:59.115
A cold what?

00:00:59.159 --> 00:01:01.423
It's a disease
my mom says people used to get.

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:02.758
Ah...

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:05.287
but humans still sneeze
for other reasons

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:07.629
and I cannot seem
to do it right.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:11.501
Ah... ah...

00:01:11.538 --> 00:01:13.972
How can you be practicing
something like sneezing

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:15.632
when we're arriving
at your home planet

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:16.972
for the first time?

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:18.477
Aren't you interested in that?

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:21.071
More than interested--
fascinated.

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:22.604
One might say agog.

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:24.981
But I also find
sneezing interesting.

00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:26.211
Choo!

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:28.948
Chh...

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:33.254
Captain Picard wishes
to see you on the Bridge.

00:01:33.293 --> 00:01:37.286
Captain, confirming Class M
reading there, but...

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:39.457
but the sensors aren't showing
any life readings...

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:40.727
not even vegetation.

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:41.995
Strange.

00:01:42.035 --> 00:01:45.801
The cruiser that found Data
reported farmlands there.

00:01:45.839 --> 00:01:48.774
Do you want to take her
into orbit, Data?

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:50.173
No, thank you, sir.

00:02:13.733 --> 00:02:16.361
Continue on
into close parking orbit.

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:17.733
Aye, sir.

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:20.261
I could say
"home, sweet home," sir

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:23.503
if I understood how the word
sweet applies.

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:25.670
It usually refers to memories.

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:28.579
It usually refers
to one's own memories, Captain.

00:02:28.615 --> 00:02:31.743
Do the memories you have
include farms, Data?

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:33.274
Affirmative, sir

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:35.583
but the colony's
principal interest was science.

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:37.783
Data, I don't understand
how you can hold

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:39.451
the memories of 41 1 people

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:42.484
if that means every experience,
every day of their life...?

00:02:42.529 --> 00:02:44.121
It does not, unfortunately.

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:47.622
It means only the knowledge
they had accumulated.

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:50.795
Actually, I'm quite deficient
in some basic human information.

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:52.202
Sneezing, for example.

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:55.173
Sneezing?

00:02:55.208 --> 00:02:56.732
Approaching close parking orbit.

00:02:56.776 --> 00:02:59.472
Assemble your away party,
Commander.

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:02.276
This must be an exciting time
for you, Mr. Data.

00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:04.647
I'm tempted to lead
the away team myself

00:03:04.684 --> 00:03:07.175
except that my first officer
would object.

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:09.814
How would Starfleet judge me
if I didn't?

00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:12.950
An entire Earth colony
did disappear down there.

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:15.722
You see?

00:03:15.762 --> 00:03:18.322
Now in close parking orbit, sir.

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:20.798
Mr. Data...

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:22.664
welcome home.

00:03:46.491 --> 00:03:51.952
Space, the final frontier.

00:03:51.997 --> 00:03:55.797
These are the voyages
of the Starship Enterprise.

00:03:55.834 --> 00:03:57.802
Its continuing mission--

00:03:57.836 --> 00:04:01.397
to explore
strange new worlds

00:04:01.439 --> 00:04:06.138
to seek out new life
and new civilizations

00:04:06.177 --> 00:04:11.581
to boldly go
where no one has gone before.

00:05:13.978 --> 00:05:16.572
First Officer's Log,
Stardate 4124.5:

00:05:16.614 --> 00:05:20.311
We have found Data's home
to be a completely dead world

00:05:20.351 --> 00:05:22.512
down to lifeless vegetation.

00:05:22.553 --> 00:05:25.113
No insects--
not even soil bacteria.

00:05:25.156 --> 00:05:26.623
What is it

00:05:26.658 --> 00:05:29.650
that could kill everything
on an entire planet?

00:05:35.166 --> 00:05:38.499
Recording signal locked
onto the Enterprise, sir.

00:05:38.536 --> 00:05:41.130
This looks like anything
but farmland.

00:05:41.172 --> 00:05:42.639
Agreed, sir.

00:05:42.674 --> 00:05:46.701
The soil appears almost
completely lifeless.

00:05:46.744 --> 00:05:49.679
This is the exact position
in the Tripoli log.

00:05:49.714 --> 00:05:51.375
Do you recognize anything, Data?

00:05:51.416 --> 00:05:53.384
The land contours are familiar.

00:05:53.418 --> 00:05:56.114
Topographically,
this is the correct area.

00:05:56.154 --> 00:05:57.451
This once was rich farmland

00:05:57.488 --> 00:05:59.217
I'd say something like
20 to 30 years ago.

00:05:59.257 --> 00:06:02.886
I was discovered 26 years ago.

00:06:02.927 --> 00:06:05.259
Commander, I'd say that
everything on this planet

00:06:05.296 --> 00:06:08.356
was either dead or dying
at the time Data was found.

00:06:08.399 --> 00:06:12.836
I was found 20 meters
in that direction, sir.

00:06:18.743 --> 00:06:20.176
Data, any idea at all

00:06:20.211 --> 00:06:23.112
why you were given
the colonists' memories?

00:06:23.147 --> 00:06:25.615
I've always felt
that it was done hurriedly

00:06:25.650 --> 00:06:26.617
but I know little more.

00:06:26.651 --> 00:06:28.278
Here, sir.

00:06:28.319 --> 00:06:31.220
This is where
the cruiser's landing party

00:06:31.255 --> 00:06:34.315
found the signal device
that led them here.

00:06:34.359 --> 00:06:38.261
And they found me lying there.

00:06:41.299 --> 00:06:44.462
You were just lying out there
in the open?

00:06:44.502 --> 00:06:47.403
No identity record,
no instructions?

00:06:47.438 --> 00:06:49.963
Only a layer of dust.

00:06:50.041 --> 00:06:52.441
What's the first thing
you remember, Data?

00:06:52.477 --> 00:06:53.705
Opening my eyes...

00:06:53.745 --> 00:06:57.977
Iooking into the eyes
of the Tripoli landing party.

00:06:58.049 --> 00:07:00.574
They believed
that the signal device

00:07:00.618 --> 00:07:03.451
sensed their presence
and activated me.

00:07:03.488 --> 00:07:06.457
Then this very spot
was your birthplace.

00:07:07.759 --> 00:07:08.987
Commander.

00:07:11.295 --> 00:07:14.287
I think I've got
this place figured out here.

00:07:14.332 --> 00:07:18.166
This was very cleverly done
to make this look

00:07:18.202 --> 00:07:20.727
Iike a natural hollow
in the terrain here.

00:07:20.772 --> 00:07:24.105
There are signs of it
being constructed in a hurry

00:07:24.142 --> 00:07:25.734
as if to hide something here.

00:07:25.777 --> 00:07:29.110
Yes, that was it, Geordi.

00:07:29.147 --> 00:07:31.172
This awakens a memory remnant

00:07:31.215 --> 00:07:34.309
of how the colonists
hoped to remain hidden

00:07:34.352 --> 00:07:37.219
but their fear
of being discovered

00:07:37.255 --> 00:07:40.588
Ied to their storing information
in me.

00:07:42.794 --> 00:07:45.285
Yeah, thought so.

00:08:14.292 --> 00:08:18.786
No life readings in here,
either, sir.

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:20.220
The colonists' laboratory--
extremely well-equipped.

00:09:20.258 --> 00:09:22.351
Does this stir
any memories, Data?

00:09:22.393 --> 00:09:24.418
Only a vague impression

00:09:24.462 --> 00:09:28.125
of some of my functions
being tested here.

00:09:31.869 --> 00:09:34.394
Posted by proud parents?

00:09:34.438 --> 00:09:39.375
It depicts something
that feels familiar, sir

00:09:39.410 --> 00:09:40.934
and dangerous

00:09:40.978 --> 00:09:44.243
but I have no idea
what it represents.

00:09:44.282 --> 00:09:46.614
And that is all

00:09:46.651 --> 00:09:49.518
except...

00:09:49.554 --> 00:09:56.687
for an impression of this
being a Dr. Soong's work area.

00:09:56.727 --> 00:09:58.661
Who?

00:09:58.696 --> 00:10:00.721
You don't mean
Dr. Noonien Soong?

00:10:00.765 --> 00:10:02.198
He was called that here

00:10:02.233 --> 00:10:03.757
but his memories indicate

00:10:03.801 --> 00:10:05.928
he traveled here
under a different name.

00:10:05.970 --> 00:10:07.562
Dr. Noonien Soong, my friend

00:10:07.605 --> 00:10:09.971
happens to have been Earth's
foremost robotics scientist.

00:10:10.041 --> 00:10:12.066
Until he tried
to make Asimov's dream

00:10:12.109 --> 00:10:13.872
of a positronic brain
come true.

00:10:13.911 --> 00:10:15.674
A positronic brain...

00:10:15.713 --> 00:10:17.442
He promised so much

00:10:17.481 --> 00:10:20.314
and then when he failed
completely

00:10:20.351 --> 00:10:22.251
Dr. Soong disappeared.

00:10:22.286 --> 00:10:25.278
Now we know he went somewhere
else to try a second time.

00:10:25.323 --> 00:10:27.917
Data, Geordi, we'll get
a close look at this lab.

00:10:27.959 --> 00:10:29.824
You and Lieutenant Worf
reconnoiter

00:10:29.860 --> 00:10:31.521
where those corridors lead.

00:10:31.562 --> 00:10:32.893
Aye, sir.

00:11:04.629 --> 00:11:07.063
Data, it's you.

00:11:07.098 --> 00:11:09.658
An epidermal mold--

00:11:09.700 --> 00:11:12.533
made to give your exterior
the desired finish.

00:11:12.570 --> 00:11:14.697
Lieutenant Yar
to Commander Riker.

00:11:14.739 --> 00:11:15.967
Come in, Lieutenant.

00:11:16.007 --> 00:11:18.373
Sir, this installation
is big enough

00:11:18.409 --> 00:11:19.637
to hold hundreds of people

00:11:19.677 --> 00:11:21.508
but all that's here now
is empty beds.

00:11:21.545 --> 00:11:22.842
Thank you, Lieutenant.

00:11:22.880 --> 00:11:25.781
Complete your record scans
and report back here.

00:11:25.816 --> 00:11:29.718
Commander Riker, looks like
some sort of storage area.

00:11:45.770 --> 00:11:48.830
How many more Datas are there?

00:11:48.873 --> 00:11:50.363
Looks like just these two.

00:11:50.408 --> 00:11:54.708
I mean, that and the real Data.

00:12:06.390 --> 00:12:08.255
Commander...

00:12:08.292 --> 00:12:11.784
can this be another me?

00:12:11.829 --> 00:12:15.492
Or possibly my brother?

00:12:15.533 --> 00:12:18.866
I honestly don't know, Data.

00:12:20.404 --> 00:12:22.668
He needs assembling.

00:12:22.707 --> 00:12:23.867
He...

00:12:27.445 --> 00:12:30.346
Data, we don't know
that this can become alive.

00:12:30.381 --> 00:12:34.784
It is very important
for me to know that, sir.

00:12:34.819 --> 00:12:38.220
I never dreamed it was possible

00:12:38.255 --> 00:12:43.283
that I might find some link
with a form like my own.

00:12:43.327 --> 00:12:44.851
Understood.

00:12:44.895 --> 00:12:47.864
We'll take it back
to the ship with us.

00:12:55.072 --> 00:12:58.530
Captain's Log,
Stardate 41242.45:

00:12:58.575 --> 00:13:00.167
Despite having only a few hours

00:13:00.210 --> 00:13:03.202
in which to explore
Data's home planet

00:13:03.247 --> 00:13:05.181
we have discovered something

00:13:05.215 --> 00:13:07.877
which may explain
Data's beginnings

00:13:07.918 --> 00:13:10.045
if we can properly assemble

00:13:10.087 --> 00:13:13.113
and communicate
with what we've found.

00:13:46.490 --> 00:13:48.788
Signal from the Captain.

00:13:48.826 --> 00:13:51.727
They need you at the debriefing.

00:13:51.762 --> 00:13:53.354
I've been most anxious to hear

00:13:53.397 --> 00:13:55.592
the chief engineer's opinion,
Mr. Argyle.

00:13:55.632 --> 00:13:57.896
Do you believe
he can be made to function?

00:13:57.935 --> 00:14:01.393
It appears to include all
the components in your body.

00:14:01.438 --> 00:14:04.407
Not that we fully understand
your construction, either.

00:14:04.441 --> 00:14:06.500
We have our top specialists

00:14:06.543 --> 00:14:09.410
working on its
construction, Mr. Data.

00:14:09.446 --> 00:14:10.936
Just one thing.

00:14:10.981 --> 00:14:14.576
Without disassembling you,
of course

00:14:14.618 --> 00:14:17.086
if we should need more...

00:14:17.121 --> 00:14:20.454
If we should need
to compare this

00:14:20.491 --> 00:14:24.120
with the way
you're put together...

00:14:27.197 --> 00:14:28.664
Bringing it up here

00:14:28.699 --> 00:14:31.099
was the right thing to do,
Number One.

00:14:31.135 --> 00:14:32.898
We were just saying, Data

00:14:32.936 --> 00:14:34.904
that if your duplicate
functions

00:14:34.938 --> 00:14:36.997
it may answer
a lot of questions.

00:14:40.144 --> 00:14:44.171
Does it appear to have, uh...

00:14:44.214 --> 00:14:46.978
all your parts?

00:14:47.050 --> 00:14:49.109
Completely, sir.

00:14:49.153 --> 00:14:50.552
Will...

00:14:50.587 --> 00:14:54.819
will we know how to turn it on?

00:14:54.858 --> 00:14:56.849
All right.

00:14:56.894 --> 00:14:58.361
All right.

00:14:58.395 --> 00:15:00.522
Legitimate questions
about any of this

00:15:00.564 --> 00:15:02.464
need not be asked
apologetically.

00:15:02.499 --> 00:15:04.126
You feel uncomfortable

00:15:04.168 --> 00:15:06.068
on aspects
of your duplicate, Data.

00:15:06.103 --> 00:15:09.163
We feel uncomfortable, too,
and for no logical reason.

00:15:09.206 --> 00:15:11.333
If it feels awkward
to be reminded

00:15:11.375 --> 00:15:13.104
that Data is a machine

00:15:13.143 --> 00:15:17.239
just remember that we are merely
a different variety of machine.

00:15:17.281 --> 00:15:20.079
In our case,
electro-chemical in nature.

00:15:20.117 --> 00:15:22.608
Let's begin to handle this
as we would do anything else.

00:15:22.653 --> 00:15:23.950
Agreed, Captain.

00:15:23.987 --> 00:15:28.048
Let's begin with you, Data.

00:15:28.091 --> 00:15:30.855
Well, sir,
a good starting point may be

00:15:30.894 --> 00:15:32.885
why was I given human form?

00:15:32.930 --> 00:15:34.921
Well, to make it easier
for humans

00:15:34.965 --> 00:15:36.933
to relate to you-- had to be.

00:15:36.967 --> 00:15:40.266
But your designer may have had
something else to prove as well.

00:15:40.304 --> 00:15:41.771
That human-shaped robots

00:15:41.805 --> 00:15:44.239
need not be clumsy or limited
in their performance.

00:15:44.274 --> 00:15:46.435
You certainly operate
as well as we do, Data.

00:15:46.476 --> 00:15:48.774
Better in some ways, sir.

00:15:48.812 --> 00:15:52.373
You might want to have
a look at this, Captain.

00:15:52.416 --> 00:15:54.543
It could be a link to the
disappearance of the colonists.

00:15:54.585 --> 00:15:56.678
It was displayed in the lab--
no doubt by proud parents.

00:15:56.720 --> 00:16:00.383
It could be just
a child's imagination

00:16:00.424 --> 00:16:03.393
but several children
did similar drawings.

00:16:03.427 --> 00:16:05.292
Dr. Crusher to the Captain.

00:16:05.329 --> 00:16:06.591
At this point, sir

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:08.723
we very much need
Mr. Data's help.

00:16:11.501 --> 00:16:13.264
He's on his way, Doctor.

00:16:18.642 --> 00:16:20.769
Is the electromagnetic
synthemometer reading

00:16:20.811 --> 00:16:22.108
positive or negative?

00:16:22.145 --> 00:16:23.612
Positive.

00:16:23.647 --> 00:16:26.115
Press your fingers there,
Doctor.

00:16:30.420 --> 00:16:32.411
There.

00:16:32.456 --> 00:16:35.357
It operates almost as a switch.

00:16:35.392 --> 00:16:38.589
And these small projections?

00:16:38.629 --> 00:16:42.065
An android alarm clock.

00:16:42.099 --> 00:16:44.624
Is that amusing?

00:16:46.470 --> 00:16:50.099
They time how long
I remain unconscious.

00:16:50.140 --> 00:16:53.974
Are you certain about us using
these heating devices, Data?

00:16:54.077 --> 00:16:56.307
I will feel nothing at all.

00:16:56.346 --> 00:16:57.506
Marvelous.

00:16:57.547 --> 00:16:59.538
It should all be a lot simpler

00:16:59.583 --> 00:17:03.075
once we see how your
circuitry's connected.

00:17:07.090 --> 00:17:09.524
I won't mention it to anyone.

00:17:09.559 --> 00:17:11.049
You have my word.

00:17:11.094 --> 00:17:14.154
If you had
an off switch, Doctor

00:17:14.197 --> 00:17:16.893
would you not keep it secret?

00:17:16.933 --> 00:17:20.232
I guess I would.

00:17:31.715 --> 00:17:35.583
Yes, notice
the microcircuitry here

00:17:35.619 --> 00:17:36.916
and here...

00:17:36.953 --> 00:17:42.289
and then another
fibroid-like connection here.

00:17:42.326 --> 00:17:44.624
Let's close up.

00:17:57.074 --> 00:17:58.507
It seemed to go well

00:17:58.542 --> 00:18:00.874
thanks to a look
inside Mr. Data

00:18:00.911 --> 00:18:03.709
but there have been no signs
of consciousness yet.

00:18:11.822 --> 00:18:14.620
It certainly is
a good match for Data, sir.

00:18:14.658 --> 00:18:17.422
Do you think so, really?

00:18:17.461 --> 00:18:20.624
I wonder which one
was made first?

00:18:20.664 --> 00:18:23.428
He was.

00:18:26.670 --> 00:18:30.401
But they found him
to be imperfect

00:18:30.440 --> 00:18:33.876
and I was made to replace him.

00:18:39.015 --> 00:18:43.577
You may call me Lore.

00:18:51.695 --> 00:18:57.156
But I am also troubled by it
describing you as imperfect.

00:18:57.200 --> 00:18:59.691
Human language gives me
difficulty, too, sir.

00:18:59.736 --> 00:19:03.069
Imperfect could mean I lack
certain abilities he possesses.

00:19:03.106 --> 00:19:04.403
Hmm, I wonder.

00:19:04.441 --> 00:19:06.136
But the point of this is

00:19:06.176 --> 00:19:08.770
whether you and it
have approximately

00:19:08.812 --> 00:19:10.439
the same capabilities.

00:19:10.480 --> 00:19:11.606
We do, sir

00:19:11.648 --> 00:19:14.116
and your referring to him
as "it"

00:19:14.151 --> 00:19:17.416
suggests that l, too,
fit into the category

00:19:17.454 --> 00:19:18.614
of a thing.

00:19:18.655 --> 00:19:22.785
Oh, uh, l... I see your point.

00:19:22.826 --> 00:19:24.817
My apologies.

00:19:24.861 --> 00:19:26.226
Gladly accepted, sir.

00:19:26.263 --> 00:19:27.821
As for Lore's abilities

00:19:27.864 --> 00:19:30.332
his use of syntax
and grammar suggests

00:19:30.367 --> 00:19:32.130
he was given human memories

00:19:32.169 --> 00:19:33.295
similar to my own.

00:19:33.336 --> 00:19:35.201
You have equal
physical strength

00:19:35.238 --> 00:19:36.296
and mental abilities?

00:19:36.339 --> 00:19:38.466
I believe so, sir.

00:19:38.508 --> 00:19:41.636
Which requires that I now
ask you a very serious question.

00:19:41.678 --> 00:19:44.146
Since the two of you

00:19:44.181 --> 00:19:46.649
are closely related
to each other...

00:19:46.683 --> 00:19:48.310
The answer, sir

00:19:48.351 --> 00:19:52.185
is that my loyalty is to you
and Starfleet, completely.

00:19:54.124 --> 00:19:55.955
Thank you, Commander.

00:19:56.026 --> 00:19:58.927
I was certain of that.

00:19:58.962 --> 00:20:00.452
And helm control is here

00:20:00.497 --> 00:20:02.692
with the ship's heading
being given in measurements

00:20:02.732 --> 00:20:03.960
we call degrees--

00:20:04.067 --> 00:20:07.195
360 of them
in a full circle this way.

00:20:07.237 --> 00:20:08.295
Then you say mark.

00:20:08.338 --> 00:20:09.669
On the nose.

00:20:09.706 --> 00:20:13.142
Which separates it from
another full 360-degree circle

00:20:13.176 --> 00:20:15.576
this way on a right angle
to this one.

00:20:15.612 --> 00:20:18.581
So, by ordering a heading
so many degrees this way

00:20:18.615 --> 00:20:20.515
and so many this way

00:20:20.550 --> 00:20:21.983
the ship can travel
any direction--

00:20:22.052 --> 00:20:23.246
all three dimensions.

00:20:23.286 --> 00:20:24.981
And the square of a hypotenuse

00:20:25.088 --> 00:20:26.646
to the right triangle...?

00:20:26.690 --> 00:20:30.990
Is equal to the sum of
the square of the other two...

00:20:31.061 --> 00:20:32.551
two something--

00:20:32.596 --> 00:20:34.427
which I once heard

00:20:34.464 --> 00:20:35.863
but never understood.

00:20:35.899 --> 00:20:37.924
All of which you will
learn more about

00:20:37.968 --> 00:20:41.665
when the Captain has approved
your being on the Bridge.

00:20:41.705 --> 00:20:43.639
Have I committed an offense?

00:20:43.673 --> 00:20:45.231
You will find that there are

00:20:45.275 --> 00:20:47.539
many rules on starships
that must be learned.

00:20:47.577 --> 00:20:49.772
You're very clever, Wesley.

00:20:49.813 --> 00:20:52.839
I now have duties
to perform, correct?

00:20:52.882 --> 00:20:55.942
Were you ever
this anxious to please, Data?

00:20:55.986 --> 00:20:57.146
Never.

00:20:57.187 --> 00:21:00.281
I judge Lore to be superior
in that desire.

00:21:00.323 --> 00:21:04.123
Because I was designed
to be so human, my brother.

00:21:04.160 --> 00:21:05.957
I enjoy pleasing humans.

00:21:06.029 --> 00:21:07.496
"My brother."

00:21:07.530 --> 00:21:11.091
That has a nice sound
to it, Data.

00:21:11.134 --> 00:21:14.467
You consider it important
to please humans?

00:21:14.504 --> 00:21:16.495
It's not important?

00:21:16.539 --> 00:21:19.838
There are many things
of importance.

00:21:19.876 --> 00:21:21.867
Some more than others.

00:21:36.059 --> 00:21:37.993
Do you realize
that Commander Riker's

00:21:38.061 --> 00:21:41.690
hypotenuse question tricked you
into showing your knowledge

00:21:41.731 --> 00:21:43.995
was greater
than you were indicating?

00:21:44.034 --> 00:21:45.968
He didn't seem that clever.

00:21:46.002 --> 00:21:47.469
I'll be more careful.

00:21:47.504 --> 00:21:50.132
You tend to underestimate
humans, my brother.

00:21:50.173 --> 00:21:53.472
Praising young Wesley
on the helm, for example.

00:21:53.510 --> 00:21:54.568
A child.

00:21:54.611 --> 00:21:56.340
He has a child's body

00:21:56.379 --> 00:21:59.473
but we have found him
to be much more.

00:21:59.516 --> 00:22:03.077
Thank you
for that information, too.

00:22:03.119 --> 00:22:06.282
You do care
about how I perform.

00:22:06.323 --> 00:22:11.317
I pledge to be worthy
of your teaching, my brother.

00:22:11.361 --> 00:22:14.353
Try not to be jealous
of my abilities.

00:22:31.381 --> 00:22:34.544
What information
are you requesting?

00:22:34.584 --> 00:22:38.543
Everything available
on a Dr. Noonien Soong.

00:22:38.588 --> 00:22:42.183
Good old "Often Wrong" Soong.

00:22:44.661 --> 00:22:46.720
A joke, brother.

00:22:46.763 --> 00:22:48.526
Actually, he was

00:22:48.565 --> 00:22:50.726
a genius by human standards.

00:22:50.767 --> 00:22:52.792
But he destroyed his reputation

00:22:52.836 --> 00:22:54.997
by making what seemed
wild promises

00:22:55.105 --> 00:22:57.335
about his positronic
brain design--

00:22:57.374 --> 00:22:59.171
almost all of which failed.

00:22:59.209 --> 00:23:03.669
Promises he later proved
to be true.

00:23:05.215 --> 00:23:08.343
Which made
you and me possible, brother.

00:23:08.385 --> 00:23:13.652
Our beloved father.

00:23:13.690 --> 00:23:15.123
Will I soon have a uniform

00:23:15.158 --> 00:23:16.625
Iike that, brother?

00:23:16.659 --> 00:23:18.559
If you get one
the way I did, Lore

00:23:18.595 --> 00:23:20.722
it will mean four years
at the Academy

00:23:20.764 --> 00:23:22.391
another three as Ensign

00:23:22.432 --> 00:23:24.900
ten or 12 on varied space duty
in the Lieutenant grades...

00:23:24.934 --> 00:23:29.928
A system designed to compensate
for limited human ability

00:23:29.973 --> 00:23:34.535
and you, brother, are beginning
to think as a human.

00:23:34.577 --> 00:23:38.411
You and I are completely
different from them.

00:23:38.448 --> 00:23:41.781
Are you truly satisfied
with the knowledge and memory

00:23:41.818 --> 00:23:45.379
of a few hundred
human colonists?

00:23:45.422 --> 00:23:48.255
Suppose it could reflect
thousands

00:23:48.291 --> 00:23:49.986
or millions

00:23:50.093 --> 00:23:51.651
or the knowledge

00:23:51.694 --> 00:23:55.323
of hundreds of millions
of life-forms of every kind?

00:23:58.067 --> 00:23:59.898
How?

00:23:59.936 --> 00:24:02.837
We will discuss that in time.

00:24:02.872 --> 00:24:06.273
And will we also discuss, Lore

00:24:06.309 --> 00:24:10.075
which of us
was constructed first?

00:24:10.113 --> 00:24:13.571
It would be foolish
to underestimate you, brother.

00:24:13.616 --> 00:24:15.743
Yes, I lied when I said

00:24:15.785 --> 00:24:18.447
you were made first,
but with good reason.

00:24:18.488 --> 00:24:21.651
Dr. Soong made me perfect
in his first attempt

00:24:21.691 --> 00:24:23.955
but he made me
so completely human

00:24:24.060 --> 00:24:26.460
the colonists became envious
of me.

00:24:26.496 --> 00:24:28.862
You lived with the colonists?

00:24:28.898 --> 00:24:31.662
Until they petitioned Soong

00:24:31.701 --> 00:24:36.900
to make a more comfortable,
less perfect android.

00:24:36.940 --> 00:24:39.238
In other words, you...

00:24:39.275 --> 00:24:41.436
brother.

00:24:43.546 --> 00:24:46.106
Haven't you noticed

00:24:46.149 --> 00:24:48.947
how easily I handle
human speech?

00:24:48.985 --> 00:24:51.146
I use their contractions.

00:24:51.187 --> 00:24:53.587
For example, I say "can't"

00:24:53.623 --> 00:24:55.318
or "isn't"

00:24:55.358 --> 00:25:00.091
and you say "cannot"
and "is not."

00:25:00.129 --> 00:25:02.324
I say tomato

00:25:02.365 --> 00:25:03.855
And you say tomahto

00:25:03.900 --> 00:25:06.460
I say potato
and you say potahto...

00:25:08.905 --> 00:25:10.532
A very old joke.

00:25:10.573 --> 00:25:14.202
But then you also have trouble
with their humor.

00:25:14.244 --> 00:25:15.677
Am I right?

00:25:17.013 --> 00:25:18.139
Quite true.

00:25:18.181 --> 00:25:21.309
I keep trying
to be more human

00:25:21.351 --> 00:25:23.182
and keep failing.

00:25:23.219 --> 00:25:26.382
Do you realize, brother

00:25:26.422 --> 00:25:31.052
I can help you
become more human?

00:25:31.094 --> 00:25:32.925
And do you realize, Lore

00:25:32.962 --> 00:25:36.159
that I am obligated
to report all of this

00:25:36.199 --> 00:25:37.928
to our ship's Captain?

00:25:37.967 --> 00:25:43.667
I assumed as much when I began
studying you.

00:25:43.706 --> 00:25:45.765
May I use this to learn more

00:25:45.808 --> 00:25:48.538
about this vessel
and its customs?

00:25:48.578 --> 00:25:50.546
Use it also to describe
for the Captain

00:25:50.580 --> 00:25:52.514
the time you spent
among the colonists

00:25:52.549 --> 00:25:55.143
including everything you know
about what happened to them.

00:25:55.184 --> 00:26:00.349
I promise a report
of great detail and accuracy.

00:26:00.390 --> 00:26:01.914
Thank you, Lore.

00:26:01.991 --> 00:26:04.653
I now have duties to perform.

00:26:08.665 --> 00:26:11.190
Unless, of course,
you need something more.

00:26:11.234 --> 00:26:15.432
I have more than I dreamed
possible, brother.

00:26:39.627 --> 00:26:43.290
Captain's Log,
Stardate 41242.5:

00:26:43.331 --> 00:26:44.958
Thanks to Lore's report

00:26:45.000 --> 00:26:47.867
we now know what happened
to the colonists.

00:26:47.902 --> 00:26:52.362
Beginning with a child's drawing
enhanced by Lore's description

00:26:52.407 --> 00:26:54.375
our computer has constructed

00:26:54.409 --> 00:26:57.071
the image
of a great crystalline entity

00:26:57.112 --> 00:26:59.876
which feeds on life,
insatiably ravenous

00:26:59.914 --> 00:27:02.678
for the life force found
in living forms

00:27:02.717 --> 00:27:06.244
capable of stripping all life
from an entire world.

00:27:06.287 --> 00:27:09.256
But how did Data
escape that thing? Or Lore?

00:27:09.290 --> 00:27:10.917
Lore had been disassembled.

00:27:10.959 --> 00:27:13.723
He explained it as jealousy
from the colonists

00:27:13.762 --> 00:27:16.094
and Data wasn't yet alive
at that time.

00:27:16.131 --> 00:27:18.292
Which explains why Data
could be left outside

00:27:18.333 --> 00:27:19.857
in no danger from that creature.

00:27:19.901 --> 00:27:21.596
Whatever happened
to the colonists

00:27:21.636 --> 00:27:22.762
he would be found

00:27:22.804 --> 00:27:24.169
by the first Starfleet crew

00:27:24.205 --> 00:27:26.070
that responded
to the signal

00:27:26.107 --> 00:27:27.074
he transmitted.

00:27:27.108 --> 00:27:28.939
By which Dr. Soong
left proof behind

00:27:29.044 --> 00:27:30.636
that his experiment did work.

00:27:30.678 --> 00:27:32.145
Captain...

00:27:32.180 --> 00:27:34.740
how believable do you find
that crystal thing?

00:27:34.783 --> 00:27:38.480
With so little of even
our galaxy explored

00:27:38.520 --> 00:27:41.045
I find it at least possible.

00:27:41.089 --> 00:27:44.354
Data, are you expecting Lore
to come up here?

00:27:44.392 --> 00:27:46.360
He left your quarters
some time ago.

00:27:46.394 --> 00:27:47.486
To go?

00:27:47.529 --> 00:27:50.362
My turbo sensors say
he went to Deck Four. Worf?

00:27:50.398 --> 00:27:53.231
Where he examined
some microminiature work tools

00:27:53.268 --> 00:27:55.133
and fine grind quadratanium.

00:27:55.170 --> 00:27:56.660
Which is used
in our construction.

00:27:56.704 --> 00:27:58.968
That particular compound
is no more suspicious, sir

00:27:59.074 --> 00:28:00.803
than a human looking
for an antiseptic

00:28:00.842 --> 00:28:02.070
or an ointment.

00:28:02.110 --> 00:28:03.702
Nevertheless,
I should check it out.

00:28:03.745 --> 00:28:05.474
You're watching
everything he does, Data?

00:28:05.513 --> 00:28:08.778
Is that the act of a brother?

00:28:08.817 --> 00:28:11.081
It's the act
of a Starfleet officer

00:28:11.119 --> 00:28:12.746
obeying his Captain, Doctor.

00:28:17.926 --> 00:28:21.692
Captain, speaking strictly
as security chief

00:28:21.729 --> 00:28:24.527
how much can you trust Data now?

00:28:29.637 --> 00:28:31.468
I trust him completely,
Lieutenant

00:28:31.506 --> 00:28:34.737
but everyone should also realize
that that was a necessary

00:28:34.776 --> 00:28:36.607
and legitimate
security question.

00:28:36.644 --> 00:28:38.874
Thank you, sir.

00:29:00.468 --> 00:29:04.700
Lesson number one
in becoming more human:

00:29:04.739 --> 00:29:08.266
You must observe
all human customs.

00:29:08.309 --> 00:29:09.776
Champagne?

00:29:09.811 --> 00:29:13.269
An ancient ritual
still practiced

00:29:13.314 --> 00:29:17.478
when they observe
events of importance.

00:29:22.991 --> 00:29:28.156
My brother, I toast
our discovery of each other.

00:29:28.196 --> 00:29:32.496
May it fill our lives
with new meaning.

00:29:36.504 --> 00:29:39.473
I have some doubts
about the value

00:29:39.507 --> 00:29:41.475
of human customs...

00:29:41.509 --> 00:29:43.636
in this...

00:29:43.678 --> 00:29:48.479
Brother...

00:29:48.516 --> 00:29:52.782
And let us toast,
also, Dr. Soong

00:29:52.820 --> 00:29:56.551
who gave me the full richness

00:29:56.591 --> 00:29:59.651
of human needs and ambitions.

00:29:59.694 --> 00:30:03.562
A perfect match for my mind,
my body.

00:30:03.598 --> 00:30:08.194
Brother... help me.

00:30:10.238 --> 00:30:15.972
And let us toast also
the great crystal entity

00:30:16.010 --> 00:30:20.379
with whom I learned
to communicate.

00:30:20.415 --> 00:30:23.282
Before Dr. Soong disassembled me

00:30:23.318 --> 00:30:26.378
I earned its gratitude
by revealing

00:30:26.421 --> 00:30:28.651
the way to the colonists.

00:30:28.690 --> 00:30:31.284
Can you imagine its gratitude

00:30:31.326 --> 00:30:34.762
when I give it the life
on this vessel?

00:30:37.765 --> 00:30:38.993
This is strange, sir.

00:30:39.099 --> 00:30:40.430
I show Commander Data

00:30:40.467 --> 00:30:42.628
transmitting on
a subspace channel.

00:30:42.669 --> 00:30:45.832
I know Data's been doing
considerable research

00:30:45.873 --> 00:30:47.966
into Dr. Soong's background.

00:30:48.008 --> 00:30:49.475
Let's be sure.

00:30:49.510 --> 00:30:54.641
Wesley, would you look in
on Commander Data, discreetly?

00:30:54.681 --> 00:30:56.342
Yes, sir.

00:31:02.089 --> 00:31:04.114
Crystal entity

00:31:04.158 --> 00:31:05.955
upon arriving here

00:31:05.993 --> 00:31:10.521
you can identify me
as the machine named Data.

00:31:12.533 --> 00:31:14.501
End of message.

00:31:14.535 --> 00:31:16.196
Come in, please.

00:31:19.740 --> 00:31:20.968
Glad you're here, Wesley.

00:31:21.074 --> 00:31:24.237
Lore suddenly attacked me
and I had to turn him off.

00:31:24.278 --> 00:31:25.973
Why did he do that, Data?

00:31:26.079 --> 00:31:29.139
He discovered
we have been using sensors

00:31:29.183 --> 00:31:30.980
to follow what he does.

00:31:32.886 --> 00:31:35.286
I practiced his facial tic.

00:31:35.322 --> 00:31:36.983
Do I have it right?

00:31:37.057 --> 00:31:39.992
I'd suggest
you forget imitating him.

00:31:40.027 --> 00:31:41.688
If you'd said

00:31:41.728 --> 00:31:44.663
we've been using the sensors
instead of we have

00:31:44.698 --> 00:31:46.962
I might have suspected
you were Lore.

00:31:47.000 --> 00:31:49.833
Yes, I do use language
more formally than Lore.

00:31:49.870 --> 00:31:51.531
Please inform the Captain

00:31:51.572 --> 00:31:54.336
I will come up on the Bridge
and report on this.

00:31:54.374 --> 00:31:56.001
Aye, sir.

00:32:56.503 --> 00:32:58.562
Wes, tell me again

00:32:58.605 --> 00:33:02.473
how Data said
he immobilized Lore.

00:33:02.509 --> 00:33:07.469
He told me he just
turned him off, Mom...

00:33:07.514 --> 00:33:09.505
uh, Doctor.

00:33:14.021 --> 00:33:15.488
Question, Mr. Data.

00:33:15.522 --> 00:33:18.719
Did you or did you not
swear me to secrecy

00:33:18.759 --> 00:33:20.488
about your off switch?

00:33:20.527 --> 00:33:22.495
A change of mind, Doctor.

00:33:22.529 --> 00:33:24.963
If I cannot trust
the Bridge crew

00:33:25.065 --> 00:33:26.089
whom can l?

00:33:26.133 --> 00:33:29.432
Captain, I'm picking up
a bogey coming in

00:33:29.469 --> 00:33:31.494
on a five o'clock tangent.

00:33:31.538 --> 00:33:33.301
It's transmitting no lD signal,
Captain.

00:33:33.340 --> 00:33:34.898
Set main viewer on that tangent.

00:33:34.942 --> 00:33:36.534
Shields up; go to yellow alert.

00:33:36.576 --> 00:33:39.670
Transmit friendly greetings--
all languages, all frequencies.

00:33:43.550 --> 00:33:45.814
I can't believe anything's
overtaking us this fast.

00:33:45.852 --> 00:33:48.320
Beautiful, isn't it?

00:33:51.792 --> 00:33:54.090
I recognize it, sir.

00:33:54.127 --> 00:33:57.585
It's the crystal image
Lore described.

00:33:59.666 --> 00:34:02.100
My God.

00:34:15.849 --> 00:34:18.079
Still no lD
being transmitted, sir.

00:34:18.118 --> 00:34:20.279
Also no answer to our inquiries.

00:34:23.290 --> 00:34:25.258
Did you get
a direct look at it?

00:34:25.292 --> 00:34:26.953
It's like a giant
snowflake crystal

00:34:26.994 --> 00:34:28.325
but much more complex.

00:34:28.362 --> 00:34:29.920
The entire
electromagnetic spectrum

00:34:29.963 --> 00:34:31.225
seems to play about inside it

00:34:31.264 --> 00:34:33.528
but I haven't the slightest
idea what it is, sir.

00:34:33.567 --> 00:34:35.762
Thank you, Lieutenant.

00:34:35.802 --> 00:34:39.863
Data, if there's anything else
that Lore could tell us about it

00:34:39.906 --> 00:34:41.601
it may be important.

00:34:41.641 --> 00:34:43.472
Can you control him enough
to question him?

00:34:43.510 --> 00:34:45.273
I will have to examine
him to know, sir.

00:34:47.247 --> 00:34:50.739
Captain, recommend
you do not let...

00:34:50.784 --> 00:34:52.752
him roam the ship freely.

00:34:52.786 --> 00:34:54.947
Ensign.

00:34:54.988 --> 00:34:57.786
Wesley is simply showing himself
to be alert and responsible

00:34:57.824 --> 00:34:59.314
something to be encouraged.

00:34:59.359 --> 00:35:01.122
Come. You can watch
everything I do.

00:35:01.161 --> 00:35:02.788
Not if I have a choice.

00:35:02.829 --> 00:35:04.592
That is enough, Ensign!

00:35:04.631 --> 00:35:05.928
When addressing
a senior officer...

00:35:05.999 --> 00:35:08.058
I've guided his training, sir.
I'm the one at fault.

00:35:08.101 --> 00:35:10.296
You will show
the proper respect.

00:35:10.337 --> 00:35:12.498
I will accompany you down there
to make certain of it.

00:35:12.539 --> 00:35:15.167
With your approval,
of course, sir.

00:35:32.893 --> 00:35:34.190
Careful of Lore.

00:35:34.227 --> 00:35:38.254
Good, he is still unconscious.

00:35:38.298 --> 00:35:42.291
Notice the same twitch
even though he is unconscious.

00:35:42.335 --> 00:35:43.962
Stay back.

00:35:44.004 --> 00:35:47.906
We may have problems if he
senses someone else is near.

00:35:52.245 --> 00:35:53.234
Lore.

00:35:55.382 --> 00:35:57.942
I have a few
questions to ask you.

00:35:57.984 --> 00:36:01.010
Lore, it is Data.

00:36:01.054 --> 00:36:02.214
He senses you.

00:36:02.255 --> 00:36:05.486
I cannot control him
if you stay.

00:36:05.525 --> 00:36:07.493
Please, I will record
everything he says.

00:36:07.527 --> 00:36:09.427
And you bring it
to the Bridge immediately.

00:36:17.938 --> 00:36:21.237
And you want to be
as stupid as them...

00:36:21.274 --> 00:36:22.764
dear brother?

00:36:38.225 --> 00:36:40.193
Well, Number One?

00:36:40.227 --> 00:36:41.785
It was Lore, sir--

00:36:41.828 --> 00:36:44.092
same facial twitches
that we've seen all along

00:36:44.131 --> 00:36:47.100
Iying unconscious on the floor
exactly as Data had described

00:36:47.134 --> 00:36:48.863
and then it suddenly
became violent

00:36:48.902 --> 00:36:50.961
apparently sensing
that Wesley and I were present.

00:36:51.037 --> 00:36:53.335
Or is it Lore pretending
to be Data and faking it all?

00:36:53.373 --> 00:36:55.273
I asked for Commander
Riker's report

00:36:55.308 --> 00:36:56.502
acting Ensign Crusher

00:36:56.543 --> 00:36:58.067
and since it now seems clear

00:36:58.111 --> 00:36:59.169
that you are unable to function

00:36:59.212 --> 00:37:00.611
within the limits
of that appointment...

00:37:00.647 --> 00:37:01.944
Captain.

00:37:10.757 --> 00:37:12.054
Deflector shields holding, sir.

00:37:12.091 --> 00:37:13.718
Bring photon torpedoes
to ready.

00:37:13.760 --> 00:37:15.227
Main phasers to ready.

00:37:15.261 --> 00:37:17.229
Go to red alert, please.

00:37:20.767 --> 00:37:22.291
Weapons now readied, sir.

00:37:22.335 --> 00:37:24.895
No, Captain, let me talk to it.

00:37:24.937 --> 00:37:27.371
You didn't say
you could do that.

00:37:32.211 --> 00:37:33.803
Affirmative. Talk to it.

00:37:33.846 --> 00:37:36.838
Open hailing frequencies.

00:37:36.883 --> 00:37:41.820
Crystal form,
I identify myself as Data.

00:37:41.854 --> 00:37:44.789
Advising you
to stop your attack.

00:37:44.824 --> 00:37:46.849
The humans here are powerful--

00:37:46.893 --> 00:37:50.124
capable of injuring
or even destroying you.

00:37:57.570 --> 00:38:00.130
Now I call that communicating.

00:38:00.173 --> 00:38:03.540
Suggest moving fast to
confirm what I told it, sir.

00:38:03.576 --> 00:38:05.544
Permission to use
the large transporter

00:38:05.578 --> 00:38:06.875
in Cargo Room Three.

00:38:06.913 --> 00:38:09.347
There I can beam up
some living pattern

00:38:09.382 --> 00:38:10.713
perhaps a large tree.

00:38:10.750 --> 00:38:13.082
Which you'll beam over
next to the entity.

00:38:13.119 --> 00:38:14.552
That is correct, Riker.

00:38:14.587 --> 00:38:17.556
Our ship's phasers will then
blast and disintegrate it

00:38:17.590 --> 00:38:20.252
proving we are dangerous.

00:38:21.427 --> 00:38:22.485
Make it so.

00:38:22.528 --> 00:38:24.052
Sir?

00:38:26.199 --> 00:38:27.564
Do it.

00:38:34.874 --> 00:38:37.570
Sir, I know this may finish me

00:38:37.610 --> 00:38:38.577
as acting Ensign...

00:38:38.611 --> 00:38:39.703
Shut up, Wesley.

00:38:42.748 --> 00:38:44.716
Lieutenant, pick
a good security team

00:38:44.750 --> 00:38:45.910
and let me know what he does.

00:38:45.952 --> 00:38:47.385
Aye, sir.

00:38:47.420 --> 00:38:49.445
"Shut up, Wesley"?

00:38:49.489 --> 00:38:51.616
Doctor...

00:38:51.657 --> 00:38:53.955
And since
I am finished here, sir

00:38:54.026 --> 00:38:55.186
may I point out...

00:38:55.228 --> 00:38:56.525
Shut up, Wesley.

00:38:56.562 --> 00:39:00.123
That everything that I have said
would've been listened to

00:39:00.166 --> 00:39:01.861
if it came
from an adult officer.

00:39:04.203 --> 00:39:07.070
Request permission
to return to my quarters, sir.

00:39:07.106 --> 00:39:10.098
Agreed. Doctor, go with him.

00:39:10.143 --> 00:39:14.876
You're putting me
off the Bridge?

00:39:14.914 --> 00:39:17.576
I'm asking you to keep
an eye on your son

00:39:17.617 --> 00:39:19.380
during all of this, Doctor.

00:39:27.927 --> 00:39:29.895
Emergency close.

00:39:31.931 --> 00:39:34.593
Now show me
your warrior fierceness.

00:39:53.786 --> 00:39:55.083
I'll look.

00:39:55.121 --> 00:39:59.581
But I shouldn't have let you
talk me into this.

00:39:59.625 --> 00:40:00.751
Mom, it's Data!

00:40:00.793 --> 00:40:02.124
He's been hurt.

00:40:05.298 --> 00:40:06.925
It's Data, Mom.

00:40:06.966 --> 00:40:09.264
I heard you know how
to turn them on.

00:40:09.302 --> 00:40:11.270
This is very serious.

00:40:11.304 --> 00:40:14.637
So just tell me
to "Shut up, Wesley"

00:40:14.674 --> 00:40:15.698
and I will.

00:40:15.741 --> 00:40:17.709
You're being very unfair, Wes.

00:40:19.078 --> 00:40:21.308
Data, the crystal thing
is outside

00:40:21.347 --> 00:40:23.212
somewhere close to the ship

00:40:23.249 --> 00:40:25.376
and Lore is loose
on the inside.

00:40:25.418 --> 00:40:27.215
How badly are you hurt, Data?

00:40:27.253 --> 00:40:31.815
I will function sufficiently
to stop Lore, Doctor.

00:40:36.229 --> 00:40:42.293
Crystal entity form,
it's your old friend.

00:40:50.610 --> 00:40:52.578
Very good.

00:40:52.612 --> 00:40:55.410
You've understood perfectly
so far.

00:40:55.448 --> 00:40:57.416
Next I will signal

00:40:57.450 --> 00:40:59.213
that I'm about to transport
something out

00:40:59.252 --> 00:41:01.243
at which time
the deflector shields

00:41:01.287 --> 00:41:03.255
will turn off for a moment

00:41:03.289 --> 00:41:05.553
and if you move in at that time

00:41:05.591 --> 00:41:06.751
it...

00:41:07.760 --> 00:41:10.251
How sad, dear brother.

00:41:10.296 --> 00:41:13.857
You make me wish
I were an only child.

00:41:22.308 --> 00:41:25.209
Then why this marvelous gift?

00:41:25.244 --> 00:41:29.544
The troublesome
little man-child.

00:41:29.582 --> 00:41:33.313
Are you prepared for the kind of
death you've earned, little man?

00:41:33.352 --> 00:41:36.947
If you take one more step
towards my son...

00:41:36.989 --> 00:41:40.254
Ah... motherhood.

00:41:43.763 --> 00:41:45.128
Back off

00:41:45.164 --> 00:41:46.859
or I'll turn your little man

00:41:46.899 --> 00:41:48.423
into a torch.

00:41:48.467 --> 00:41:50.935
I promise him exquisite pain

00:41:50.970 --> 00:41:53.438
unless you obey me, too,
brother.

00:41:53.472 --> 00:41:54.564
Move away, Data.

00:41:54.607 --> 00:41:56.165
Please.

00:41:56.208 --> 00:41:58.768
Do you see now

00:41:58.811 --> 00:42:02.747
the advantages
of being completely human?

00:42:02.782 --> 00:42:05.216
It includes kindness.

00:42:05.251 --> 00:42:08.414
I give you your life, Doctor.

00:42:08.454 --> 00:42:10.422
Go quickly

00:42:10.456 --> 00:42:13.653
and I may not injure
your son at all.

00:42:13.693 --> 00:42:15.854
I will stay with Wesley, Doctor.

00:42:15.895 --> 00:42:16.919
Go!

00:42:16.962 --> 00:42:18.623
Or he'll be shrieking

00:42:18.664 --> 00:42:20.632
by the count of five.

00:42:20.666 --> 00:42:22.258
One

00:42:22.301 --> 00:42:23.495
two

00:42:23.536 --> 00:42:25.970
three

00:42:26.072 --> 00:42:27.972
four...

00:42:28.074 --> 00:42:32.408
Thank you for my
human qualities, Dr. Soong.

00:42:32.445 --> 00:42:33.434
Wait!

00:42:34.480 --> 00:42:38.348
A small payment
for your son's misdeeds.

00:42:55.601 --> 00:42:56.898
Wes, the transporter.

00:43:05.211 --> 00:43:06.542
Wesley, now!

00:43:24.897 --> 00:43:28.162
Lore's gone, sir. Permanently.

00:43:34.907 --> 00:43:39.207
Doctor, now that Wesley's safe,
go to Sick Bay at once.

00:43:39.245 --> 00:43:42.908
Captain, that crystal thing
has begun to move away.

00:43:52.925 --> 00:43:55.860
Data, you all right?

00:43:55.895 --> 00:43:58.295
Yes, sir, I'm fine.

00:44:00.199 --> 00:44:02.133
Then get rid
of that damned twitch

00:44:02.168 --> 00:44:03.897
and put on a correct uniform.

00:44:03.936 --> 00:44:05.733
Yes, Captain.

00:44:05.771 --> 00:44:08.899
Ensign Crusher,
you able to return to duty?

00:44:08.941 --> 00:44:09.908
Yes, sir.

00:44:09.942 --> 00:44:11.068
Then do so

00:44:11.110 --> 00:44:13.738
and let the Bridge know
that all is well down here.

00:44:13.779 --> 00:44:14.939
Aye, sir.

00:44:18.951 --> 00:44:20.475
It's gone, sir.

00:44:20.519 --> 00:44:22.578
Without Lore,
it had no way to reach us.

00:44:22.621 --> 00:44:24.851
And we're overdue
for our computer refit.

00:44:24.890 --> 00:44:27.484
Number One,
have you ever considered

00:44:27.526 --> 00:44:29.460
whether Data is more human

00:44:29.495 --> 00:44:31.463
or less human
than we want?

00:44:31.497 --> 00:44:34.091
I only wish we were all
as well-balanced, sir.

00:44:34.133 --> 00:44:35.725
Agreed.
